==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|goh|spīwan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*spīwaną}}, from {{inh|de|ine-pro|*(s)ptyēw-||to spit, vomit}}. Compare Dutch {{m|nl|spuwen}}, {{m|nl|spugen}}, English {{m|en|spew}}, Danish {{m|da|spy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃpaɪ̯ən/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-speien.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-strong|class=1|speit|spie|gespien|past participle 2=gespieen}}

# to [[spit]]
# {{label|de|euphemistic}} to [[vomit]]

====Conjugation====
* The past participle currently has two different pronunciations: one corresponding to {{m|de|gespien}} and the other to {{m|de|gespieen}}. Today, though, the only official spelling is {{m|de||gespien}}, regardless of pronunciation.
* Similary the conjunctive (subjunctive) is spelled {{m|de|spiee}} or {{m|de|spie}}. Both are pronounced [ˈʃpiːə], but only the latter spelling is official nowadays.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|spit}} {{l|de|spucken}}
* {{sense|vomit}} {{l|de|kotzen}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|de|Wasserspeier}}
* {{l|de|Speispinne}}

